WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.230
What’s up guys, my name is Colin McNeil for theScore
esports.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:11.680
Ya know, in CS:GO, there are few things in more
satisfying than a good AWP kill.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:17.820
Whether it’s a 200 IQ wallbang, a dirty no-scope or a sick flick,  I feel like I could watch

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.030
these highlights all day.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:25.900
So you know what, let's go ahead and do just that with the Top 10 AWP kills in CS:GO.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:35.160
Coming in at number 10 is Stewie 2k’s epic
3k to force OT in the final map of the ELEAGUE

00:00:35.179 --> 00:00:38.000
Boston Major Grand Finals.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:01:01.000
(Casting)

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:09.500
There are many different ways an AWP can be
effective, but the difference between average

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:15.970
and amazing plays lies right here, at number
nine as Dupreeh hits an insane 2-man collateral

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.000
through the smoke.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:33.260
(Casting)

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:39.920
Bodyy comes in at number eight on our list as he displays his creative abilities with the now infamous

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.369
“Bodyy Wallbang”.

00:01:41.369 --> 00:01:46.280
After pulling it off in back to back rounds
against Astralis, Bodyy not only shocked viewers

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:51.000
at home, but also French and American casters
on stream.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:09.680
(Casting)

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.340
But that’s not where it ends, Bodyy went
on to re-create the same kill in another match

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.000
versus Mousesports, leaving the crowd chanting
his name.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:34.320
(Casting)

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:40.420
Number seven goes to Fnatic’s JW who stood up and
asserted his dominance making sure all eyes,

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:41.510
were on him.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.560
In an effort to take B-site with a minute
left on the clock, SK ran into the wrong man,

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.000
at the wrong time.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:03:11.120
(Casting)

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.960
Known as one of the best AWPers to ever play
the game, KennyS is no stranger to highlight

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:18.099
reel plays.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:25.000
At number six, Kenny puts on an absolute clinic for
the crowd in a 1v3 clutch at Dreamhack London.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:53.360
(Casting)

00:03:54.860 --> 00:04:00.500
One of the only players in CS:GO to serve
as both primary AWPer and in-game leader , Fallen

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:07.000
shows us why he is among the best of the best
in this 2v5 clutch in our No. 5 play.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:05:25.460
(Casting)

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:32.660
At number four, Guardian shows us why he is one of
best players to ever pick up the AWP.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:38.140
With just 19 seconds left on the clock, Guardian
puts on a one-man show as he dances around

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:41.900
pillar, wiping out an onslaught of Mousesports
players coming from

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.200
all directions.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:06:13.480
(Casting)

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:20.960
Our number three play sees Nifty go on an absolute
tear with three VAC worthy shots killing three

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:27.000
Tyloo players during the second map of the
Boston Major Asia Minor’s grand final.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.080
Oh, and each one of them was a wallbang.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:07:26.840
(Casting)

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:32.960
Coming in at number two on our list is S1mple,
who, in a 1v2 against Fnatic with 30 seconds

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:39.650
left, drops down from the heavens to no-scope
both Dennis and Krimz to win the round.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:44.300
This play was so good that it earned S1mple
a graffiti tag on the map as a tribute to

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.620
this unforgettable moment.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:08:11.000
(Casting)

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:17.340
Blowing past the competition at number one
on our list is none other than Coldzera’s

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.460
legendary jumping AWP.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:24.430
Recognized as one of the most iconic AWP kills
in the game, Coldzera puts a quick end to

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:30.000
Team Liquid’s B-rush with a 4K that could
only be described as devine.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:09:03.960
(Casting)

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:14.580
Ok guys, that was our list. But if you have a god-like AWP kill that you think we missed, don't be afraid to flame us...I mean tell us in the comments section below.

